WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.444 --> 00:00:04.277
(oriental instrumental music)

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.131
- [Voiceover] The Shaolin monks of China

00:00:07.131 --> 00:00:10.810
are an ancient order
surrounded in mystery.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.537
They spend their lives learning kung fu

00:00:12.537 --> 00:00:14.537
and Buddhist philosophy.

00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:31.762
- [Voiceover] After defecting
from communist China,

00:00:31.762 --> 00:00:34.805
one Shaolin monk found
himself living in New York,

00:00:34.805 --> 00:00:37.425
training some unique clients
ranging from movie stars

00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:39.008
to hip hop artists.

00:01:18.973 --> 00:01:21.272
- [Voiceover] As Shi Yan
Ming's popularity grew,

00:01:21.272 --> 00:01:23.046
his teachings began
attracting the attention

00:01:23.046 --> 00:01:27.129
of one of New York's most
famous hip hop artists.

00:01:28.792 --> 00:01:30.042
- Just a train.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.182
- [Voiceover] The shifu has spent years

00:01:34.182 --> 00:01:36.372
training with RZA from Wu-Tang Clan,

00:01:36.372 --> 00:01:38.638
even going so far as to
appear in the music video

00:01:38.638 --> 00:01:40.346
for Shaolin Temple.

00:01:40.346 --> 00:01:43.429
(inaudible speaking)

00:01:55.918 --> 00:01:58.000
- [Voiceover] But Shi Yan
Ming strongly believes

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.355
that the benefits of Shaolin

00:01:59.355 --> 00:02:02.188
can be adapted for any individual.

00:02:27.837 --> 00:02:31.670
(peaceful instrumental music)

